> ISO 27001:2022 §6.1.2 — Information security risk assessment and treatment.
> P×I (Probability × Impact) scoring. Review at least annually or after significant architecture changes.

---

## Probability × Impact Matrix

| Probability \ Impact | Low (1) | Medium (2) | High (3) | Critical (4) |
| -------------------- | ------- | ---------- | -------- | ------------ |
| **Unlikely (1)**     | 1       | 2          | 3        | 4            |
| **Possible (2)**     | 2       | 4          | 6        | 8            |
| **Likely (3)**       | 3       | 6          | 9        | 12           |
| **Almost Certain (4)** | 4     | 8          | 12       | 16           |

### Risk Classification Thresholds (ISO 27001 A.8.2)

| Score | Tier     | Response SLA                                        |
| ----- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |
| ≤ 4   | Low      | Monitor; review at next quarterly cycle             |
| 5–8   | Medium   | Mitigate within 90 days; add to backlog             |
| 9–12  | High     | Mitigate within 30 days; notify security lead       |
| > 12  | Critical | Immediate action; escalate to management            |

